('CMCX.L', '2021-01-26', 'HL', '(Sharecast News) - Financial services company CMC Markets has selected Amazon Web Services to help d', 'CMC Markets selects Amazon Web Services to aide digital transformation', '(Sharecast News) - Financial services company CMC Markets has selected Amazon Web Services to help deliver the next phase of its digital transformation.\r\nCMC Markets said the adoption of AWS would provide it with the \"agility, security and resiliency\" to deliver on its ambitious product development pipeline by freeing up \"valuable development hours\", taking its delivery time from six months to six weeks and allowing clients to benefit from faster access to its new product innovations.\n\r\nThe FTSE 250-listed firm stated that with a raft of new products set to be launched in 2021, the enhanced infrastructure would play \"a critical role\" in ensuring new and existing customers will receive the highest quality service.\n\r\nChief technology officer Brendan Foxen said: \"Over the last ten years, our product offering, trades executed and volumes of data have grown considerably.\n\r\n\"Adopting AWS and using the highest levels of abstraction and native services allows us to develop our product offering with a far greater speed and richness of customer experience, underpinned by the scale and reliability of AWS services.\"\n\r\nAs of 0850 GMT, CMC Markets shares were up 1.18% at 387.0p.'),
('CMCX.L', '2021-01-20', 'HL', '(Sharecast News) - Online trading platform CMC Markets said on Wednesday that full-year net operatin', 'CMC Markets sees FY net operating income at top end of consensus', '(Sharecast News) - Online trading platform CMC Markets said on Wednesday that full-year net operating income is set to be at the upper end of market expectations following a continued strong performance, underpinned by high client income retention.\r\nConsensus for net operating income for the full year 2021 is between £370.2m and £387.5m.\n\r\nIn an update for the period from 1 October 2020 to 31 December, CMC said the business has continued to perform \"very well\", with high active client numbers resulting in strong client trading activity, albeit at lower levels than earlier in the financial year.\n\r\nIn addition, client income retention remained well above 80%, but below the levels reported for H1 2021, as guided.\n\r\nCMC said its investment in platform technology continues to attract and retain premium clients, with \"market leading functionality and robust operational performance\".\n\r\n\"This was especially evident during the November Pfizer vaccine announcement when our platforms remained resilient and performed very well,\" it said. \"The business reported no outages during this very volatile trading period.\"\n\r\nChief executive Peter Cruddas said: \"I\'m delighted by our performance, and as we enter our final financial reporting quarter, we are focusing on delivering on our premium client strategy through technology, service and a resilient trading platform. In addition, we have a healthy pipeline of projects that will drive new revenue streams, which I will talk more about in the next financial year.\"'),
('CMCX.L', '2020-11-23', 'HL', '(Sharecast News) - CMC Markets revealed on Monday that deputy chief executive David Fineburg and his', 'Director dealings: CMC Markets deputy CEO lowers stake', '(Sharecast News) - CMC Markets revealed on Monday that deputy chief executive David Fineburg and his spouse Victoria had disposed of 253,857 ordinary shares in the FTSE 250-listed trading platform operator.\n\r\nFineburg, who was appointed to the board back in 2014, sold the shares on Thursday at an average price of 390.0p each, for a total value of £990,042.\n\r\nJust last week, CMC Markets reported a record first-half performance as it benefited from ongoing volatility related to the Covid-19 pandemic.\n\r\nIn the six months ended 30 September, pre-tax profit surged 369% to £141.1m, with net operating income up 126% to £230.9m.\n\r\nAs of 1650 GMT, CMC shares were up 4.73% at 421.0p.\n\r\nTop Director Buys\n\r\nMenzies(john) (MNZS)\r\nDirector name: Gomez-Reino,Alvaro\r\nAmount purchased: 50,000 @ 161.66p\r\nValue: £80,830.00\n\r\nNaked Wines (WINE)\r\nDirector name: Devlin,Nicholas\r\nAmount purchased: 3,892 @ 508.75p\r\nValue: £19,800.55\n\r\nSeeing Machines Ltd. (SEE)\r\nDirector name: Carmichael,Les\r\nAmount purchased: 375,000 @ 4.00p\r\nValue: £15,000.00\n\r\nSeeing Machines Ltd. (SEE)\r\nDirector name: Kang Ng,Yong\r\nAmount purchased: 375,000 @ 4.00p\r\nValue: £15,000.00\n\r\nSeeing Machines Ltd. (SEE)\r\nDirector name: Hill,Kate\r\nAmount purchased: 375,000 @ 4.00p\r\nValue: £15,000.00\n\r\nInternational Consolidated Airlines Group Sa (cdi) (IAG)\r\nDirector name: Campuzano,MarÃ­a Fernanda MejÃ­a\r\nAmount purchased: 10,679 @  1.54\r\nValue:  14,844.77\n\r\nValeura Energy Inc Npv (di) (VLU)\r\nDirector name: Guest,Sean \r\nAmount purchased: 60,500 @ 24.00p\r\nValue: £14,520.00\n\r\nHenderson International Income Trust (HINT)\r\nDirector name: Walker,Lucy\r\nAmount purchased: 6,750 @ 148.34p\r\nValue: £10,012.61\n\r\nInternational Consolidated Airlines Group Sa (cdi